# One line ending for the whole repository.
#
# Without this file the ending of a tracked text file is whatever the run
# that last wrote it happened to use, and the repository drifted into
# holding both: the 1.0.0a5 commit rewrote 23 files from LF to CRLF while
# the files it did not open stayed LF, and a release diff then reported
# 25,113 insertions against a real 2,741. A diff nobody can read without
# --ignore-cr-at-eol is a release nobody can review.
#
# LF is the choice because this package is published to PyPI and its
# sources are read on every platform. Git checks the same bytes out on
# Windows, where every editor and every tool in the toolchain reads LF
# without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# the two images, which git must copy byte for byte. text=auto detects
# them on its own; naming them is cheaper than relying on that
*.gif binary
